% NY N336228 (2023-2024): a men's upper body garment.
scenario ny_n336228 is:
    style TSUBLCK002 is an upper body garment,
        as stated in ruling NY N336228 at "TSUBLCK002 is a men’s upper body garment constructed from 100% cotton".
    style TSUBLCK002 is classified under the US tariff,
        as stated in ruling NY N336228 at "Harmonized Tariff Schedule of the United States (HTSUS)".
    the fabric construction of style TSUBLCK002 is knitted,
        as stated in ruling NY N336228 at "waffle knit fabric".
    the cut of style TSUBLCK002 indicates men,
        as stated in ruling NY N336228 at "TSUBLCK002 is a men’s upper body garment constructed from 100% cotton".
    style TSUBLCK002 has an opening starting at the neckline,
        as stated in ruling NY N336228 at "partial front opening with three button closures on the placket".
    style TSUBLCK002 closes left over right,
        as stated in ruling NY N336228 at "a left-over-right".
    style TSUBLCK002 contains 100 percent of cotton,
        as stated in ruling NY N336228 at "TSUBLCK002 is a men’s upper body garment constructed from 100% cotton".
    style TSUBLCK002 is claimed to belong to sleepwear,
        as stated in ruling NY N336228 at "you refer to Style TSUBLCK002 as sleepwear and state that the garment will be sold as part of coordinating separates".
    the claim that style TSUBLCK002 belongs to sleepwear is rejected,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N336228 at "these garments are not classified as sleepwear",
        because "garments of this style and construction are multi-use loungewear worn in informal situations in and around the home, not garments designed for wear only to bed".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of style TSUBLCK002 is 6105.10"].

